{
  "abstract": "Can a multi-layer causal Transformer be trained without a backward pass—with zero reverse pullbacks, zero VJP helpers, and zero same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while improving speed and short-horizon accuracy over matched-subset node-perturbation comparators? We study a 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) pipeline across 108 backward-free multi-seed arms (`exp26`–`exp48`, plus 7 local-pullback and 13 exact-backpropagation references; $128$ arms $=383$ runs) on development-only `DEV`/`VAL-B` splits of ClimbMix `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$720$ steps) and Native `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$ steps). We analyze stream-partitioned WM for separable channels and `RMSNorm` interfaces (Proposition 1), commute $W_v$ with causal attention during the forward pass to lift `attn.c_v` cosine alignment $8.2\\times$ ($+0.1104\\to+0.9069$, Proposition 2), route lexical credit via a diagonal skip surrogate (Proposition 3), and bound the expected same-token `RMSNorm` post-install residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Proposition 4). Fused Triton kernels cut the 13-matrix `d6` WM suite $38.4\\times$ ($134.31\\to3.50$ ms) and `fwd+rule` step time $8.33\\times$ ($155.6\\to18.68$ ms). On 4-matrix `d6` ($24.58\\text{M}$ active parameters), co-designed `Pre-Polar Muon`, embedding velocity, and drift annealing reach $2.0682\\pm0.0006$ `DEV` BPB (vs. $2.0532$ 4-matrix Backpropagation, $2.2603$ $K=16$ local node perturbation, and $2.2415$ 76-draw suffix-recomputed node perturbation). Extending to 5-matrix Spherical Active-$W_Q$ (`exp45`) reaches $2.0641\\pm0.0006$, and full 6-matrix ($26.35\\text{M}$, $100\\%$ active) decoupled $(W_Q,W_K)$ with $\\gamma_K=0.85$ future-query key credit (`exp47`) reaches $2.0631\\pm0.0008$ ($M=1$) and **$2.0595\\pm0.0007$ `DEV` BPB ($M=2$ amortized local probes)**. At fixed 100 steps on Native `50.3M`, isolated Triton substitution speeds up `fwd+rule` $1.44\\times$ (`exp32`) and $6.33\\times$ ($M_g=1$, `exp43`), reaching $1.8978\\pm0.0007$ `DEV` BPB on 4 matrices, $1.8897\\pm0.0008$ on 5-matrix Active-$W_Q$ (`exp46`, $9.80$ GiB), and **$1.8884\\pm0.0007$ ($M=1$, $10.08$ GiB) and $1.8853\\pm0.0013$ `DEV` BPB ($201.21$ PPL, $10.24$ GiB) on full 6-matrix Active-$(W_Q,W_K)$ at $M=2$ (`exp48`, $99.999\\%$ active)**, vs. 6-matrix $1.6989$ backpropagation.",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Extended backward-free 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) from 5-matrix Active-W_Q to full 6-matrix (100% active matrix parameters) joint (W_Q, W_K) attention routing and amortized multi-probe (M=2) local Stage-1 probing across 11 new 3-seed arms (33 new runs; total 128 multi-seed arms = 383 runs across Seeds 46, 47, 48): (a) On ClimbMix d6 (exp47_d6_6mat_joint_qk_results.json, 26.35M / 26.35M = 100% active matrix parameters), an 8-point discount sweep gamma_K in {0.00..1.00} and 8-arm 3-seed study resolve the exp45 coupled same-pos failure (2.0669) via decoupled forward query/key displacement probes (-0.0014 BPB main effect) and discounted future-query key credit at gamma_K = 0.85, eta_K = 0.012, beta_K = 0.98 (-0.0015 BPB main effect), reaching 2.0631 +- 0.0008 DEV BPB (288.64 PPL) at M=1 and 2.0596 +- 0.0008 (or 2.0595 +- 0.0007 DEV BPB, 2.0227 +- 0.0008 VAL-B, 285.81 PPL with isolated RNG) at M=2 (-0.0087 BPB vs. 4-matrix WM 2.0682; within +0.0063 BPB of 4-matrix Exact BP 2.0532). (b) On Native 50,332,176 (T=2,048, exp48_native50m_6mat_active_qk_results.json, 99.999% active parameters), full 6-matrix Decoupled Active-(W_Q, W_K) reaches 1.8884 +- 0.0007 DEV BPB (202.96 PPL) at M=1 in 5,116.3 ms/step (10.08 GiB VRAM) and 1.8853 +- 0.0013 DEV BPB (1.8722 +- 0.0012 VAL-B, 201.21 PPL) at M=2 in 5,806.4 ms/step (10.24 GiB VRAM; -0.0125 BPB / -7.18 PPL vs. 4-matrix exp43 1.8978; -0.0044 BPB vs. 5-matrix exp46 1.8897 at fixed 100 steps). 2. Resolved all 5 v4 acceptance review suggestions: added 3-seed unprojected Euclidean Active-W_Q control (2.0649 +- 0.0006); stated the conditional first-order key identity with O(sigma) remainder; framed exp44 scale_factor=8.0 (96.9%) and eps=1e-4 (+0.0288 BPB) as descriptive decompositions; credited Dust [9] Sec. 2.3 and general_pretraining_18/v8 [5]; and reconciled Table 7 3-seed mean timings (2195.2/3817.7/6012.9 ms for exp46), approximate BF16 inverse-RoPE recovery, and fixed-token vs. equal-compute comparisons.",
